{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1529972-time-of-judgment-20th-anniversary-editions","id":1529972,"title":"Time of Judgment, 20th Anniversary editions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-04T11:53:41-08:00","id":1529972,"title":"Time of Judgment, 20th Anniversary editions","content":"This is intended as a companion piece to the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1529949-time-of-judgment-retrospective-20-years-later\">Time of Judgment Retrospective: 20 Years Later</a> thread. With the 20th Anniversary lines mostly shut down (I think M20 still has a couple of books in the works, companions to <b>Lore of the Traditions</b>; but that's it) and the 5e lines shifting to a reboot model (H5 and W5 are explicitly reboots, and V5 is now being treated as one as well), we're seeing something not unlike the shift from the original World of Darkness to the new World of Darkness that took place 20 years ago; only this time, the old World of Darkness is just\u2026 stopping. So what I'm thinking of looking at in this thread is the idea of updating the Time of Judgment to the present. <br /> <br /> When the 20th Anniversary editions first came out, the Time of Judgment was \u201cdecanonized\u201d, alongside with most of the metaplot. In V20, the Week of Nightmares was made optional; W20 make no mention of Anthelios or of the Stargazers' departure from the Concordiat; M20 makes the Avatar Storm something that might or might not have happened, and if so might or might not still be happening; Wr20 flat out ignores <b>End of Empire</b>. Only C20 embraced what few developments happened from 1999 to 2003 in their entirety. This means that there's always the option of adding all of that right back in; only, it's happening <i>now</i>. <br /> <br /> But I'd rather take a slightly different tac. Instead of treating ToJ20 as an <i>ending</i>, how about treating it as a <i>transformation</i>? Have <b>Vampire</b>'s Gehenna scenario focus less on ending the world and more on setting up a post-Gehenna setting for the Kindred. For <b>Werewolf</b>, draw some inspiration from the Norse myth of Ragnarok: the world ends, as we know it; the fatalism of the prophecies cannot be denied. But it's followed by a rebirth into a literal post-Apocalypse setting \u2014 possibly with the birth of a new Gaia to replace the one that the Wyrm destroyed, and hints of the beginnings of a generations-long restoration of the Wyrm to its original role. <b>Mage</b>'s Time of Judgment might feature rampant and blatant supernatural phenomena shattering Technocratic Reality Zones and flipping them to Localized Zones almost overnight; modern society has been ravaged, but the Awakened now have more freedom to act than ever before. <b>Wraith</b> gets its Sixth Great Maelstrom, only with the Stormwinds subsiding and the beginnings of a new society of the dead beginning to form in the aftermath of Stygia's fall. And <b>Changeling</b> enters the Endless Winter with the return of the Fomorians and the Dreaming becoming hostile to the Kithain. <br /> <br /> We never got around to 20th Anniversary editions of <b>Hunter</b>, <b>Mummy</b>, <b>Demon</b>, or <b>Orpheus</b>. These lines could be re-envisioned as <i>spinning out of </i>the new Time of Judgment instead of leading up to it: in the wastelands following the end, the Messengers start Imbuing mortals with the power to combat the Fallen who were recently released from the Abyss; and Osiris recalls the Reborn and transforms them into the Amenti as survivors from the fall of Orpheus begin to explore the ruins of both the worlds of the living and the dead. <br /> <br /> Overall, go with a mood of <i>desperate hope</i>: the worst has happened, and the world has hit rock bottom; but we've survived. The only choice remaining is whether to wallow in the ruins until we die, or to start the arduous task of reclaiming what we've lost. <br /> <br /> As well, present this as a \u201cday after tomorrow\u201d notion: the world isn't ending <i>today, </i>but at an unspecified time in the relatively near future. When you're good and ready to move on past the modern day to a post-Apocalyptic world, <i>then</i> implement the Time of Judgment; until then, keep playing the X20 games as is. <br /> <br /> At least, that's <i>my</i> pitch. What would you do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T07:36:44-08:00","id":1530024,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd love to see some TOJ 20th Anniversary books for the Storyteller's Vault at least <br /> <br /> And I'm flattered my thread inspired you to make this one as a companion piece","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T01:28:43-08:00","id":1530349,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the reboot element of the three lines is something they will rapidly back pedal and isn't going to remotely reflect future supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T06:48:14-08:00","id":1530377,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how, considering the fundamental structural differences that exist between HtR vs. H5 and WtA vs. W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T09:04:29-08:00","id":1530381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1529972-time-of-judgment-20th-anniversary-editions?p=1530349#post1530349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think the reboot element of the three lines is something they will rapidly back pedal and isn't going to remotely reflect future supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without a mandate from higher than the Creative Dev, and it seems unlikely that anyone in that position knows or cares about this tiny little wing of their financial empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T11:40:34-08:00","id":1530392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1529972-time-of-judgment-20th-anniversary-editions?p=1530377#post1530377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how, considering the fundamental structural differences that exist between HtR vs. H5 and WtA vs. W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Retcons are not reboots even if you change something fundamental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T06:34:30-08:00","id":1530439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1529972-time-of-judgment-20th-anniversary-editions#post1529972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least, that's <i>my</i> pitch. What would you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me the Times of Judgement are defined by my relationship with Apocalypse and Ascension. The former expects for the pillars of heaven to shake and for an apocalypse to be a change that is irreversible - once the Apocalypse has happened we're done, pack up your toys and that's it. If anything does come afterwards it is so different that it is in no way, shape or form similar to the Our World But Weird.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Ascension doesn't really care, the endgoal and the playstyle of Mage never really expected people to indulge in the end of the world fixation that many of the other games had. It's a war that will always be fought for yourself and who you are and for being the avatar of change. For that reason, I felt that Ascension as a book failed me - I wanted better tools to explore the themes of Ascension, not a bunch of doomsday plots.<br /> <br /> So what to do with them? If there was an opportunity to approach these things again, I would love for there to be an actually book about myriad forms of Ascension (without a singular anwser on what it really is). I feel that Werewolf's end book has aged the best, and while we could adapt elements of the storylines to more resonate with the modern day, I feel it might be more fruitful to approach this with NEW earth-shattering doomsday scenarios - maybe something about the Fera going crazy, for instance with Rokea bringing horrors from the depths and seeking to drown the world and purify Land with Sea or with the Mnesis wars which could decide if the past ever came to be. Maybe something about technology and man running away from what the Weaver intended and an apocalypse being man enslaving the Weaver?<br /> <br /> Wraith had Ends of the Empire instead of a Time of Judgement book, what if it's TOJ book was Seeds of an Empire and brought tools to bring different new setups and kingdoms for building up your own lands of the dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T09:24:42-08:00","id":1530456,"title":"","content":"I fully endorse <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a>'s concept for Ascension 20th Anniversary Edition; but bear in mind that one of the concepts of Ascension sometimes addressed in MtA is <i>Mass Ascension</i>; and if any of <i>those</i> are achieved, the setting will be fundamentally changed. So even a book that deals primarily with the concept of Ascension would have a section in it about how Ascension can be played as an end-of-the-world scenario. The catch is that that would be just one section of a book that likely devotes just as much or more page-count to personal Ascension that ends an <i>individual </i>mage's story instead. It would still fundamentally be a book about endings, though; just not so focused on the <i>world</i> ending.<br /> <br /> And yeah; though it came five years earlier, I likewise tend to treat <b>Ends of Empire</b> as Wraith's Time of Judgment book; and I'd agree with your notion of a \u201chow to build your own kingdoms of the Dead\u201d book \u2014 though I'd also want to give it an appendix that takes the Orpheus appendix in Wr20 and suggests possibilities for how some post-Stygian settings might involve more prominent interactions between the Underworld and the Skinlands, with at least one such scenario having Orpheus come into its own. <br /> <br /> So, what would you do for Gehenna 20?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T14:59:30-08:00","id":1530672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1529972-time-of-judgment-20th-anniversary-editions?p=1530456#post1530456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully endorse <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a>'s concept for Ascension 20th Anniversary Edition; but bear in mind that one of the concepts of Ascension sometimes addressed in MtA is <i>Mass Ascension</i>; and if any of <i>those</i> are achieved, the setting will be fundamentally changed. So even a book that deals primarily with the concept of Ascension would have a section in it about how Ascension can be played as an end-of-the-world scenario. The catch is that that would be just one section of a book that likely devotes just as much or more page-count to personal Ascension that ends an <i>individual </i>mage's story instead. It would still fundamentally be a book about endings, though; just not so focused on the <i>world</i> ending.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutley. That is also a possible way how Ascension can go, after all they did liberally lift from the Human Instrumentality Project for one of the Mage Doomsday scenarios. However, I do feel that's incredibly narrow-minded in just focusing on that. Awakening and Ascension are mostly personal things ladden with symbolism, self-exploration and handling your own demons and becoming more than you ever believed you could be. It's not simple for most people to engage with such a topic and it has always been a weak point of Mage - to the point that many tables just ignore Seekings and settle for simple XP expenditures. I do the other way around - at my table raising Arete is free, but seekings are complicated and tailored to each character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1529972-time-of-judgment-20th-anniversary-editions?p=1530456#post1530456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah; though it came five years earlier, I likewise tend to treat <b>Ends of Empire</b> as Wraith's Time of Judgment book; and I'd agree with your notion of a \u201chow to build your own kingdoms of the Dead\u201d book \u2014 though I'd also want to give it an appendix that takes the Orpheus appendix in Wr20 and suggests possibilities for how some post-Stygian settings might involve more prominent interactions between the Underworld and the Skinlands, with at least one such scenario having Orpheus come into its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Orpheus was a great take on the worlds of the dead, and I feel that their writing team could have done some really cool stuff by giving us more tools to create different expressions and narrative weights for the Lands of the Dead. I would have also loved to have seen more about letting go and coming to terms with your baggage. Wraith is such an amazing game that is all about learning to let go and to deal with the damage you left in the world behind you. Getting stuck in the predatory Realm politics and conflicts is a fail state for those who cannot come to term with life. Anything that gave more support to catharsis and moving on would be a great chapter in a book like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1529972-time-of-judgment-20th-anniversary-editions?p=1530456#post1530456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what would you do for Gehenna 20?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a rather antagonistic relationship with Vampire, I know it very well and have way too many books for it, but the core assumptions of the game do not resonate with me. In many ways I saw Gehenna as rather on point for the self-indulgent nature of Vampire. There would definitely need to be support for this style of play and this style of ending, but I would prefer to see some new things - possibly leaning into the fact that Scholars of the Gehenna of the Whip and Fedora persuasion has been a longterm staple of Vampire, but usually reserved just for the Signature characters.<br /> <br /> Why not make this into a whole style of discovering what the Gehenna actually is, possibly in a format similar to Night's Black Agents Dracula Dossier (*) in which the players get to be the explorers and collectors of Nodist lore, figuring out the secret history of Vampires, getting to evade and interact with legendary figures and yet lead into a plethora of different endings, some of which may be a whimper and some of which may be a bang.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (*) Dracula Dossier is Kenneth Hite's Toolbox freeform mega campaign. Based on the full text of Dracula it reinterprets the history, the people, the places, the items and the organizations to multiple time periods and to different importance/irrelevance/redharringness. It has an excellent set of tools to build your own campaign with the key elements of the Dracula lore and to make it your own, whether you would like to make it about spies, aliens, gothic heroes or Hitler's Blood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}